{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "b1a9d4e2-7c53-4f18-9a6d-blog0api0v1",
    "name": "Blog API v1",
    "description": "Laravel blog API.\n\n**Quick start**\n1. Import this collection and `blog-api.postman_environment.json`.\n2. Select the \"Blog API - local\" environment.\n3. Hit **Run Collection** \u2014 every request passes top to bottom.\n\nLogin captures `{{token}}` automatically; `{{post_slug}}` and `{{comment_id}}` are captured too.\n\n**Notes**\n- Auth is a Sanctum bearer token, set at collection level. Public endpoints override to \"No Auth\".\n- Any request carrying a **file** must be `POST` with `_method=PUT` \u2014 PHP only populates `$_FILES` on POST.\n- Background jobs power thumbnails, emails and cache refreshes. Run a worker:\n  `php artisan queue:work --queue=images,mail,cache,default`\n- Rate limits: register 5/min, login 20/min per IP, password 5/min per user, verification 6/min, others 60/min. `429` means you hit one.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Unique email per run so Register never collides.",
          "const setVar = (k, v) => { pm.collectionVariables.set(k, v); try { pm.environment.set(k, v); } catch (e) {} };",
          "if (!pm.variables.get('run_id')) { setVar('run_id', Date.now().toString().slice(-6)); }"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "base_url",
      "value": "http://localhost:8000",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "token",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "post_slug",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "comment_id",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "email",
      "value": "demo@example.com",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "password",
      "value": "password-secret",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "run_id",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Auth",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Register",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/register",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "register"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Public. Creates a user and queues a verification email.\n\n**201** returns the user \u2014 no token, call Login next.\n\n`name` 2-255 \u00b7 `email` unique, lowercased \u00b7 `password` min 8 (12 + mixed case/numbers/symbols in production), `confirmed`.",
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Postman Tester\",\n  \"email\": \"postman+{{run_id}}@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"password-secret\",\n  \"password_confirmation\": \"password-secret\"\n}"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const setVar = (k, v) => { pm.collectionVariables.set(k, v); try { pm.environment.set(k, v); } catch (e) {} };",
                  "pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const b = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (b.data && b.data.email) { setVar('email', b.data.email); setVar('password', 'password-secret'); }"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Login  \u2192 captures {{token}}",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/login",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "login"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Public. Exchanges credentials for a bearer token.\n\n**201** `{ message, token, token_type, data }` \u2014 the test script stores `token`.\n\n`device_name` is optional; it labels the token. Unverified accounts CAN log in. Wrong password and unknown email return the same `422` so accounts can't be enumerated. 5 failed/min per email+IP \u2192 `429`.",
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{email}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{password}}\",\n  \"device_name\": \"postman\"\n}"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const setVar = (k, v) => { pm.collectionVariables.set(k, v); try { pm.environment.set(k, v); } catch (e) {} };",
                  "pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const b = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('returns a token', () => pm.expect(b.token).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty);",
                  "setVar('token', b.token);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Current user",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/user",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "user"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Requires a token.\n\n**200** `{ data: { id, name, email, email_verified, email_verified_at, avatar_url, avatar_thumbnail_url, created_at } }`"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Resend verification email",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/email/verification-notification",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "email",
                "verification-notification"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Public. Queues a fresh verification link.\n\n**202** \u2014 identical response whether the address is unknown, known, or already verified, so it can't reveal which emails have accounts.\n\nLimits: 6/min per IP, 3/min per email.",
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{email}}\"\n}"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Verify email (signed link \u2014 read the description)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/email/verify/:id/:hash?expires=&signature=",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "email",
                "verify",
                ":id",
                ":hash"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "expires",
                  "value": "",
                  "description": ""
                },
                {
                  "key": "signature",
                  "value": "",
                  "description": ""
                }
              ],
              "variable": [
                {
                  "key": "id",
                  "value": "1"
                },
                {
                  "key": "hash",
                  "value": ""
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "**This URL cannot be built by hand** \u2014 it is cryptographically signed; any edit invalidates it (`403`).\n\nCopy the whole link from the email. With `MAIL_MAILER=log` it lands in the log:\n\n```bash\ngrep -o 'http[^\"]*email/verify[^\"]*' storage/logs/laravel.log | tail -1\n```\n\n**200** on success and again if already verified (different `message`). Expires after 60 minutes.",
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Profile",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Update profile (name / email)",
          "request": {
            "method": "PUT",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/user/profile",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "user",
                "profile"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Requires a token. `PATCH` works identically. Both fields optional \u2014 send only what changed; sending neither is a valid no-op.\n\n**Changing the email resets verification** and queues a new link; `email_verified` returns `false`. Re-sending your existing address changes nothing.\n\n**Changing the name** queues a job that clears your name from every cached post byline:\n```bash\nphp artisan queue:work --queue=cache\n```\n\nAvatars live on this same endpoint \u2014 see the two requests below.\n\n**200** `{ message, data }`.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Updated Name\",\n  \"email\": \"{{email}}\"\n}"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Update profile (multipart, with avatar)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/user/profile",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "user",
                "profile"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Requires a token. **Method is POST with `_method=PUT`** \u2014 a real multipart PUT arrives with no file in PHP.\n\n**Pick a file for `avatar` before sending** (Postman can't store file paths in an export).\n\nRules: jpg/jpeg/png/webp, real MIME checked (SVG rejected), min 100\u00d7100, max 2 MB. The filename is never trusted.\n\n`avatar_thumbnail_url` returns `null` \u2014 a 200px thumbnail is generated in the background, which also refreshes your avatar on every cached byline:\n```bash\nphp artisan queue:work --queue=images,cache\n```\n\nOther profile fields can ride along in the same request.\n\n**200** `{ message, data }`.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "formdata",
              "formdata": [
                {
                  "key": "_method",
                  "value": "PUT",
                  "type": "text",
                  "description": "Required \u2014 PHP only parses multipart on POST"
                },
                {
                  "key": "name",
                  "value": "Updated Name",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "key": "avatar",
                  "type": "file",
                  "src": [],
                  "description": "JPG/PNG/WebP \u00b7 min 100\u00d7100 \u00b7 max 2 MB"
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Remove avatar",
          "request": {
            "method": "PUT",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/user/profile",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "user",
                "profile"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Requires a token. Clears the picture and deletes both files from disk.\n\nCombining `remove_avatar` with an `avatar` file is rejected (`422`) \u2014 they contradict each other. A no-op when no avatar is set.\n\n**200** with both avatar URLs `null`.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"remove_avatar\": true\n}"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Change password",
          "request": {
            "method": "PUT",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/user/password",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "user",
                "password"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Requires a token **and** your current password \u2014 a stolen token alone can't lock you out.\n\nOn success **all your other tokens are revoked**; the token making this request survives, so Postman stays authenticated. The new password must differ from the current one. Limit: 5/min per user.\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f This really changes the password. The test script updates `{{password}}` so later Logins keep working.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"current_password\": \"{{password}}\",\n  \"password\": \"a-brand-new-secret\",\n  \"password_confirmation\": \"a-brand-new-secret\"\n}"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const setVar = (k, v) => { pm.collectionVariables.set(k, v); try { pm.environment.set(k, v); } catch (e) {} };",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "  const sent = JSON.parse(pm.request.body.raw.replace(/{{password}}/g, pm.variables.get('password')));",
                  "  setVar('password', sent.password);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Posts",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "List posts  \u2192 captures {{post_slug}}",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/posts?page=1&per_page=15",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "posts"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "page",
                  "value": "1",
                  "description": "1-1000"
                },
                {
                  "key": "per_page",
                  "value": "15",
                  "description": "1-50, default 15"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Public, newest first, served from cache.\n\n**200** `{ data, links, meta }`. Each post carries `comments_count`, `tags[]`, `author { id, name, avatar_url }` and both image URLs.\n\n`page`/`per_page` are capped because each combination is its own cache key; out-of-range \u2192 `422`.",
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const setVar = (k, v) => { pm.collectionVariables.set(k, v); try { pm.environment.set(k, v); } catch (e) {} };",
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const b = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (b.data && b.data.length) { setVar('post_slug', b.data[0].slug); }"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Show post",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/posts/{{post_slug}}",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "posts",
                "{{post_slug}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Public. Looked up by **slug**, not id. Served from cache.\n\n**200** `{ data }` \u00b7 **404** unknown slug.",
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Create post (JSON, no image)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/posts",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "posts"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Requires a token.\n\n`title` 3-255 \u00b7 `description` min 10 \u00b7 `tags` optional, max 10, each 2-50 chars, matched by slug so `Laravel` and `laravel` are one tag.\n\nThe slug is generated from the title and de-duplicated (`-2`, `-3`).\n\n**201** `{ message, data }`.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"title\": \"A Post From Postman\",\n  \"description\": \"A description that is comfortably longer than the ten character minimum.\",\n  \"tags\": [\"laravel\", \"postman\"]\n}"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const setVar = (k, v) => { pm.collectionVariables.set(k, v); try { pm.environment.set(k, v); } catch (e) {} };",
                  "pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const b = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (b.data && b.data.slug) { setVar('post_slug', b.data.slug); }"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Create post (multipart, with image)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/posts",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "posts"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Requires a token. **Select a file for `image` before sending.**\n\nRules: jpg/jpeg/png/webp, real MIME checked (SVG rejected), \u2265200\u00d7200, \u22645 MB. Filenames are never trusted.\n\nThe 600px thumbnail is generated in the background, so `image_thumbnail_url` is `null` in the response:\n```bash\nphp artisan queue:work --queue=images\n```\n\nNote the repeated `tags[]` keys \u2014 that is how arrays travel in multipart.\n\n**201** `{ message, data }`.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "formdata",
              "formdata": [
                {
                  "key": "title",
                  "value": "A Post With A Cover Image",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "key": "description",
                  "value": "A description that is comfortably longer than the ten character minimum.",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "key": "tags[]",
                  "value": "laravel",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "key": "tags[]",
                  "value": "images",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "key": "image",
                  "type": "file",
                  "src": [],
                  "description": "JPG/PNG/WebP \u2265200\u00d7200, \u22645 MB"
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const setVar = (k, v) => { pm.collectionVariables.set(k, v); try { pm.environment.set(k, v); } catch (e) {} };",
                  "const b = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 201 && b.data) { setVar('post_slug', b.data.slug); }"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Update post (JSON, no image)",
          "request": {
            "method": "PUT",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/posts/{{post_slug}}",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "posts",
                "{{post_slug}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Requires a token. **Author only** \u2014 editing someone else's post returns `403`.\n\nAll fields optional. `tags`: key omitted \u2192 unchanged \u00b7 `[]` \u2192 cleared \u00b7 list \u2192 replaced.\n\nThe **slug never changes**, so existing links keep working.\n\n**200** `{ message, data }`.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"title\": \"An Edited Title From Postman\",\n  \"description\": \"An edited description, still comfortably over the minimum length.\",\n  \"tags\": [\"laravel\", \"editing\"]\n}"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Update post (multipart, replace image)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/posts/{{post_slug}}",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "posts",
                "{{post_slug}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "\u26a0\ufe0f **POST with `_method=PUT`**, not a real PUT \u2014 PHP only populates `$_FILES` on POST.\n\nReplacing the image deletes the previous file and its thumbnail, and clears `image_thumbnail_url` until the job regenerates it.\n\n**Known limitation:** you cannot clear *all* tags in the same request as an image upload \u2014 multipart can't express an empty array. Use the JSON variant to clear tags.\n\n**200** `{ message, data }`.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "formdata",
              "formdata": [
                {
                  "key": "_method",
                  "value": "PUT",
                  "type": "text",
                  "description": "Required \u2014 see description"
                },
                {
                  "key": "title",
                  "value": "Edited With A New Cover",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "key": "image",
                  "type": "file",
                  "src": [],
                  "description": "JPG/PNG/WebP \u2265200\u00d7200, \u22645 MB"
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Comments",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "List comments",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/posts/{{post_slug}}/comments?page=1&per_page=20",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "posts",
                "{{post_slug}}",
                "comments"
              ],
              "query": [
